  "content": {
    "id": "v2-727073-p8-practice-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Decide which polynomial in each pair has a repeated zero.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-727073-p8-practice-slot-2-slot-2-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A(x)=x^3-x^2-8x+12$ and $B(x)=x^3+2x^2-5x-6$, which both have a zero at $x=2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A(x)$ has the repeated zero $x=2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A(2)&=8-4-16+12=0\\\\A'(x)&=3x^2-2x-8\\\\A'(2)&=12-4-8=0\\\\B(2)&=8+8-10-6=0\\\\B'(x)&=3x^2+4x-5\\\\B'(2)&=12+8-5=15\\ne0\\end{align*}$$Only $A(x)$ has $A(2)=A'(2)=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-727073-p8-practice-slot-2-slot-2-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$S(x)=x^3-3x^2-9x+27$ and $T(x)=x^3-3x^2-9x+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$S(x)$ has the repeated zero $x=3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}S'(x)&=T'(x)=3x^2-6x-9\\\\&=3(x-3)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$A repeated zero must satisfy $x=3$ or $x=-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S(3)&=27-27-27+27=0\\\\S(-1)&=-1-3+9+27=32\\\\T(3)&=27-27-27+5=-22\\\\T(-1)&=-1-3+9+5=10\\end{align*}$$Only $S(3)=S'(3)=0$, so $S(x)$ has the repeated zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-727073-p8-practice-slot-2-slot-2-q-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$M(x)=x^4-4x^3+27$ and $N(x)=x^4-4x^3+10$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$M(x)$ has the repeated zero $x=3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}M'(x)&=N'(x)=4x^3-12x^2\\\\&=4x^2(x-3)\\end{align*}$$A repeated zero must satisfy $x=0$ or $x=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}M(0)&=27\\\\M(3)&=81-108+27=0\\\\N(0)&=10\\\\N(3)&=81-108+10=-17\\end{align*}$$Only $M(3)=M'(3)=0$, so $M(x)$ has the repeated zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      }
    ]
  },
